%% DocPilot - Gmail OAuth connect flow  [NEW]
%% Read-only (gmail.readonly). One connection per (user, organization).
%% The callback has no JWT: identity comes from a one-time, hashed, 10-minute state value.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant FE as React SPA (Gmail page)
    participant API as DocPilot API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant G as Google

    U->>FE: click Connect Gmail
    FE->>API: POST /organizations/ORG/gmail/oauth/start (JWT, any member)
    alt GMAIL_CLIENT_ID or GMAIL_REDIRECT_URI missing
        API-->>FE: 503 Gmail OAuth is not configured
    else configured
        API->>DB: INSERT gmail_oauth_states (SHA-256 of random state, user, org, expires in 10 min)
        API-->>FE: authorization_url (scope gmail.readonly, access_type offline, prompt consent)
        FE->>FE: remember organization id in sessionStorage
        FE->>G: browser redirect to Google consent screen
        U->>G: approve read-only access
        G->>API: GET /gmail/oauth/callback?code=...&state=... (browser redirect, no JWT)
        API->>DB: UPDATE gmail_oauth_states SET consumed_at WHERE unconsumed AND not expired RETURNING user, org
        alt state invalid, expired or already used
            API-->>U: 400 Invalid or expired Gmail authorization state
        else user denied access (error parameter)
            API-->>U: 303 redirect to FRONTEND_URL/?gmail=cancelled
        else code present
            API->>G: exchange code for tokens (httpx, 15 s timeout)
            G-->>API: refresh token, scopes, Google email
            Note over API: 502 if Google fails. 400 if a NEW connection gets no refresh token.
            API->>API: Fernet-encrypt refresh token (503 if GMAIL_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY missing)
            API->>DB: upsert gmail_connections (UNIQUE user + org), status = active
            API-->>U: 303 redirect to FRONTEND_URL/?gmail=connected&organization_id=ORG
            U->>FE: SPA reads the query string, shows a notice, opens the Gmail page, cleans the URL
        end
    end

    Note over API,G: Later calls: decrypt the stored refresh token, ask Google for a short-lived access token (never stored), then call the Gmail API. If Google says the grant is revoked or expired, status becomes reauth_required and the API returns 401.
    Note over API,DB: Not present: a disconnect endpoint, token revocation at Google, cleanup of expired oauth state rows.
